{
  "title": "RecipeVersionSupport.revertRecipe manually reconstructs an OpenAPI \
RequestBuilder",
  "description": "`Ramekin/RecipeVersionSupport.swift:133-163` copy-pastes the \
generated-client plumbing (path templating, `APIHelper`, `JSONEncodingHelper`, \
`requestBuilderFactory.getNonDecodableBuilder`) to issue a `PUT \
/api/recipes/{id}` with a custom `RevertRecipeRequest`. This will silently \
drift from the generated code when the OpenAPI spec changes (e.g. new required \
fields). Options: (1) add a revert endpoint to the OpenAPI schema and \
regenerate; (2) serialize the existing `UpdateRecipeRequest` with the same \
nil-vs-missing semantics and call `RecipesAPI.updateRecipe`; (3) at minimum \
write an extension method in Shared and centralize the handrolled plumbing so \
one file changes when regeneration shifts.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
